      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{602d3bd675defb333e431d1b|full_name}: for that VRChat has kind of already decided that access permissions are only evaluated on entry.\n\nActually with the recent change to friends+ portal being unlocked, you can tag along to another friends+ instance and anyone can enter, even if you only had one friend and they left hours ago...\n\nFor changing instance type I could see it being fine for like going friends+ to invite+ kind of locking down. Being able to open up instance could run into TOS issues. What if you're doing something in private and it's not exactly private any more? This third paragraph is more a response to the main question. But I don't want to post twice.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
