      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: And I think that is why dropping a new portal is a good solution. People aren't \"forced\" into a situation that they did not join or dropped from one they did join.\n\nOne of the goals of a user interface is not too expand it needlessly. Particularly for the 1 in a 1000 case. I don't know for instance how often such an \"on the fly\" type change would be used, I'll guess not too often.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
